# Copy to engine/.env for local runs (never commit). Everything here has a
# working default, so an empty .env is a valid one — the nightly GitHub Actions
# workflow sets only AIENGJOBS_DB and relies on defaults for the rest.
#
# Keep this list in step with engine/src/config.ts.

# --- storage ---------------------------------------------------------------

# SQLite database. Defaults to engine/data/aiengjobs.db; the workflow points it
# at $GITHUB_WORKSPACE/data/aiengjobs.db so the cache and release steps can
# find it.
# AIENGJOBS_DB=

# Where `export` writes the site snapshot (defaults to site/src/data/snapshot.json).
# SNAPSHOT_OUT=

# --- classifier ------------------------------------------------------------
# A local ONNX encoder. There is no API key and no network call: `ingest`
# aborts before touching a feed if the model is missing, rather than degrading
# to title heuristics on a far weaker rule. See ml/README.md.

# Directory holding the exported model + tokenizer (defaults to ml/model).
# AIENGJOBS_ENCODER_DIR=
# Model filename within that directory.
# AIENGJOBS_ENCODER_FILE=
# Intra-op threads for onnxruntime. Defaults to the core count.
# AIENGJOBS_ENCODER_THREADS=
# Decision threshold, calibrated in ml/. Changing it re-scopes the whole board.
# AIENGJOBS_ENCODER_THRESHOLD=

# --- ingest ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Delay between sources, in ms (default 400 — Lever publishes a crawl-delay).
# INGEST_DELAY_MS=
# Postings processed concurrently per source (default 2). Raising this does not
# parallelise inference; ORT serialises run() on the shared session.
# INGEST_CONCURRENCY=
# Wall-clock ceiling on the polling loop, in ms (default 200 minutes). Past the
# budget `ingest` stops starting new sources and exits 0, so an overrun costs
# one night's coverage instead of being killed at the workflow's 300-minute
# timeout — which would discard the database with it.
# INGEST_BUDGET_MS=

# --- site + notifications --------------------------------------------------

# Canonical origin and base path used to build absolute URLs.
# SITE_ORIGIN=
# SITE_BASE=

# IndexNow. The key is public by design — it only proves host control, and its
# twin is served from site/public/<key>.txt.
# INDEXNOW_KEY=
# INDEXNOW_ENDPOINT=
